#X text 291 290 These 3 messages control the excution of the unstet process. The play message is applied imeadately \, the stop and pause is applied only at the the of a period. Normaly these messages are not needed \, as the unstat process starts playing automatically. You can prevent this by starting the process as "unstet -n".;
#X text 54 666 bang;
#X text 283 669 periodend;
#X text 357 668 zuklusend;
#X text 437 667 playstart;
#X text 511 668 playstop;
#X text 414 495 When Pd and unstet run on the same computer \, these messages are not needed \, as the defaults are ok. When they are on different computers \, replace *localhost" with the IP of the computer running unstet and send the connect message.;
#X text 58 36 The unstet-abraction receives (several) bangs form a running unstet process \, and can optionaly alter the process parameters or can control the execution of the process. The unstet process should be startet bevor the Pd process with the command "unstet".;
#X text 24 15 [unstet-abstraction]- integrates external unstet process;
#X msg 106 203 variation 0 0 0 0 800 1600 2400 4000;
#X msg 153 254 teiler 2 3 5 8 13;
#X msg 59 152 periode 5000 5000 13000;
#X text 505 34 The messages "periode" \, "variation" and "teiler" alter the default parameters in a unstet process. When your happy with the defaults there is no need to use these messages. You can use these messages anytime \, but the changes are applied only at the end of a period.;
#X text 309 261 The "teiler" can any have length.;
